From: haroldxie <xiewenhao2308@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: mm: export __vmalloc_node_range_noprof() for the
 KJIT huge-arena experiment

EXPERIMENT (exp/huge-arena), not for merge as is. The KJIT runtime wants
one 2 MiB chunk of read-only, executable memory that is mapped by a single
PMD block (VM_ALLOW_HUGE_VMAP, PAGE_KERNEL_ROX), which execmem_alloc()
cannot ask for on arm64 (EXECMEM_BPF is PAGE_KERNEL with 4 KiB pages, and
change_memory_common() refuses VM_ALLOW_HUGE_VMAP areas, so the 4 KiB path
cannot be converted afterwards). Export the allocator that takes the
protection and the vm flags. GPL-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mm/vmalloc.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/mm/vmalloc.c b/mm/vmalloc.c
--- a/mm/vmalloc.c
+++ b/mm/vmalloc.c
@@ -4101,6 +4101,7 @@ void *__vmalloc_node_range_noprof(unsigned long size, unsigned long align,
 
 	return NULL;
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(__vmalloc_node_range_noprof);
 
 /**
  * __vmalloc_node - allocate virtually contiguous memory
-- 
2.43.0
